nce that groundswell started  so you just it almost seems silly to  talk  in advance about well what is going to  happen next because we have seen how  quickly these things change you know to  the point where I think it was the Big  East tournament they called it off at  halftime of the first game the NBA we've  seen players pulled off the floor as  they were about to start a game this is  happening so quickly that I won't  believe it's the start of the league  year until it's the start of the league  year regardless of what they're saying  now because everything is changing so  fast as we try to wrap our arms around  this global pandemic yeah and the clue  is hiding in plain sight when the NFL  says no plans to delay the start of free  agency that means that the plans can and  will change and it's just unfortunate  that so many people in the media will  just push that because there are people  who believe it hey free agency next week  let's go I was on radio with Joe Rose in  Miami a little while ago and he was like  all right hey we're gonna have free  agency next week it's like Joe it ain't  happenin next week it's not happening  and you know there's a deeper issue here  where I think the NFL has blown an  opportunity to lead at a time when and  I'm gonna straight orde the third rail  of talking about politics but I think  most of us would agree that we are  suffering from a dearth of leadership  from our governmental entities right now  especially at the federal level all the  way up to the top and we've relied upon  our private institutions to step in and  provide the leadership and in the sports  world all of them did except the NFL and  I don't want to hear oh it's really not  our football season so we didn't have to  move look the NFL benefits from it being  football season all year long there's  playing season there's non playing  season the NFL is always front and  center and you know I I wish in  hindsight we had seen Roger Goodell on  NFL Network or somewhere else making a  clear strong statement that this is a  serious problem and we have events in  the offseason and we are as a right now  pulling the plug on everything  reassessing and then we'll let you know  as time passes what we are going to do  and I understand that if they're going  to continue with the draft for example  going to talk about that coming up they  have plans they need to follow through  on but  I just think that MDS to the extent that  people have not yet taken this seriously  and I'd like to think that the NBA  suspending its season was the moment  that people did take it seriously when I  see a full Pepsi Center last night in  Denver for a post Malone concert I  wonder what the hell those people are  paying attention to other than the fact  that well we bought the tickets let's go  to the show I mean are they not  listening are they not taking it  seriously and I feel like every major  institution in our country should be at  the forefront of getting people's  attentions and in that regard the NFL  had an opportunity and it either  negligently or intentionally squandered  it yeah I I actually thought there was a  time just a few days ago when the NFL  would come out and just say effective  immediately and until further notice no  one is getting on a plane for any  official NFL business not to go Scout  players not to bring players into your  facility have to go to pro days not for  free agent visits we're just not doing  it because we recognize the severity of  the situation we're facing and the NFL  has have done that the statements from  teams have just come in in dribs and  drabs a team will sail we're pulling our  scouts this team will say we're pulling  our coaches but not our scouts this team  will say we're letting our staff work  from home it should have just been a  league wide policy that a until we have  a better sense of what this situation it  is and how soon we can get it under  control  it's just gonna be a league wide policy  no travel for any type of league  business and I I was surprised I thought  we'd hear it like Monday and the NFL  would be leading the way now it's Friday  and whatever the NFL does next they'll  be well behind Major League Baseball the  NBA Major League Soccer the NHL the  English Premier League all the other  sports organizations and especially the  NCAA have taken significant steps that  the NFL for some reason is holding off  on taking and Sherine Williams and I  talked about this earlier damn PFT live  for me the canary in the coal mine was  the  meetings because it's been obvious for a  week now there was no way they were  gonna gather 32 owners many of whom are  in the high-risk category for a negative  outcome the ultimate negative outcome  from kovat 19a ka the coronavirus with  media and everything in a social setting  is just wasn't gonna happen it's not  gonna happen  why are they waiting to announce that  it's not gonna happen what in the world  is going on and it just tells me that  they've made the conscious decision or  the the unconscious decision to just  wait as long as possible to act and it  is a squandered opportunity to lead and  right now free agency it isn't happening  next week and I hope I'm right because  if I'm wrong and it happens it's it's  gonna cause me to view the NFL far  differently than I view the NFL right  now cuz it should not happen this is not  the time for multi-million dollar deals  to be done and hey the facilities are  all closed right if I'm a guy who's  going out as an owner of a team and  spending all this money on a free agent  I want to get the full benefit of that  contract which includes bringing the guy  to town having the press conference  holding up the Jersey and making it a  big deal and if we can just wait a few  weeks and do it later then wait a few  weeks and do it later they delayed free  agency MDS nine years ago until August  all because of what was a fairly  ordinary labor dispute well these are  ext